      en: "A former Dutch fort on a hill in Butre, offering spectacular views of the bay. Built in 1656. Good defensive position. Center of the Butre trade treaty. A ruin today. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Ghana — a country shaped by its Atlantic coastline, the Volta river system, the legacy of the Ashanti Kingdom, and its cocoa and gold wealth — and offers insight into the regional identity. Located in the West African state of Ghana along the Gulf of Guinea coast."
